## A first calculation

Import the package:

```{code-cell} python
import {{ module_name }}

{{ module_name }}.__version__
```

GC content is the fraction of a DNA sequence made up of guanine and cytosine.
Give {{ module_name }} a sequence and it returns that fraction:

```{code-cell} python
sequence = "ACGTACGTGGCC"
gc = {{ module_name }}.gc_content(sequence)
gc
```

Bases recorded as `N` are unknown, so they are left out of the calculation
rather than counted against it:

```{code-cell} python
{{ module_name }}.gc_content("GGCCNNNN")
```

If a sequence contains something that is not a DNA base, the package says so
instead of returning a misleading number:

```{code-cell} python
:tags: [raises-exception]

{{ module_name }}.gc_content("ACGT-ACGT")
```

